; personality.xon -- what this bundle IS.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every other
; manifest in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon).  A form a reader does
; not know is a loud error, never a skip.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (personality "NAME")        the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a REQUIREMENT, not a taste
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (entry "FILE")              the one self-booting file

(personality "sweet")

; HELIUM, derived rather than preferred.  The reader types are built from plain
; closures over the catalog's `type`, `buf` and `io` prims, all of which x-core
; provides; nothing here reaches for a float, a socket, or a file.
;
; The 2024 tree declared otherwise by implication -- sweet-base.x opened with
; (include "lang/r7rs/lib/r7rs-base.x"), so the smallest personality of the
; five depended on the two largest.  That was a dependency on the Scheme ALIAS
; layer, not on R7RS: see sweet/scheme.x, which is the eight names the specs
; actually use and is meant to be deleted when x-r5rs lands as a bundle.
(dialect he)

; PAIRING, NOT PINNING.  A digest freezes bytes; it says nothing about whether
; those bytes still run against a platform that moved.  Compared for EQUALITY,
; never parsed -- the platform's own rule for release strings.
(requires-release "0.5.2")

(entry "run.x")
